7075	{"artifactId":"LLD-b47dadc7cf0cccb1-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-b47dadc7cf0cccb1-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-18T14:25:28.143Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Story trailers, coverage eligibility and evidence-based normalization target the ISSUE's three stated root causes.","evidence":"Read ISSUE.md and the corresponding implementations. storyChangeSet currently retains every ordinary first-parent commit; grounding emits every entity; coverage explicitly instructs an empty testsReaching to produce HIGH. The proposed changes address those mechanisms, with legacy attribution and whole-file graph review explicitly retained as limits. [files: docs/standalone/scope-code-review-story-s-own-E20261017b47dadc7/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts]","action":"Implement the attribution and coverage changes together across both execution paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Committed review scope currently includes other Stories' ordinary first-parent commits, and BUILD persistence defaults to HEAD.","evidence":"storyChangeSet enumerates 'rev-list --first-parent --reverse --parents' over base..HEAD and retains non-merge commits without identity filtering. changedFiles intersects the net range with those paths. persistBuildRecord uses 'const commit = rec.body.commit ?? headShortSha(repoPath)'. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed trailer filter and shared BUILD persistence change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Coverage currently receives non-code/test entities and treats missing graph edges as HIGH, including synthetic diff rows.","evidence":"assembleCodeReviewGrounding pushes a summary for every entity; isTestFile filters callers only. buildDiffSymbols emits kind:'file' with testsReaching: []. buildCoveragePrompt says 'a changed symbol with an EMPTY testsReaching is a not-exercised gap — report it HIGH'. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts]","action":"Apply eligibility only to coverage and explicitly suppress symbol grading in degraded mode.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Coverage requires changes in both the daemon judge path and the controller prompt/result-injection path.","evidence":"runCodeReview calls slot.judge(subject, grounding, provider). The controller independently calls buildCoveragePrompt and injects validated results through replacement judge slots. Both handler.ts and code-review-rpc.ts independently assemble degraded grounding and replace changedFiles. These are the seams identified by the design. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"Pass groundingMode into the controller prompt emitter as well as JudgeSlot, and normalize controller coverage before injected results reach the verdict fold.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Ordinary two-parent upstream merges exclude merged-in changes while retaining merge edits; explicit BUILD commits override derivation.","evidence":"storyChangeSet computes the parents' auto-merge tree, then retains only auto..merge-commit differences; octopus merges explicitly use first-parent..merge-commit instead. persistBuildRecord applies the supplied commit before merging prior records. Existing story-commits and build-record tests assert these behaviors. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/story-commits.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/build-record.test.ts]","action":"Keep these branches and regression assertions when adding trailer attribution.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed four evidence classes preserve defined behavior when the Story has no usable test record.","evidence":"testRecordView explicitly returns null for an absent record and produces unverified states for malformed file entries. The current prompt treats pass-states as unverified. Section 4 permits no-edge-no-tests only when a record exists, but the design supplies no alternative class for an edge-free symbol with a null record, while requiring every prepared symbol to have a class. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/test-record-view.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts]","action":"Specify the null-record and malformed-record classification and normalization outcomes explicitly, and add assertions for both.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every acceptance criterion has an executable regression test that fails without this fix.","evidence":"The acceptance table specifies relevant future scenarios for ac1–ac5, but repository searches found none of the named new attribution, eligibility, normalization or trailer suites. Existing story-commits and coverage tests exercise current behavior, including accepting scripted HIGH findings without normalization. Their bodies do not establish the proposed regressions, and no tests were executed. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/story-commits.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/build-record.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/__tests__/coverage.test.ts]","action":"Implement the mapped suites and demonstrate their failure against the old behavior, including both execution paths, null records, reverted Story files and explicit BUILD commit overrides.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":2},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-18T14:25:28.143Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
